course: dictionary
lesson: 9172
title: Snuff: one word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, so read the words around it. Snuff can be a verb, a noun, or part of a phrase. «She snuffed out the candle before bed.» A candle has a flame, so to snuff it out means to put the flame out.
explain: Snuff can also mean to stop something suddenly. «The rain snuffed out our hopes of a picnic.» You cannot really put out a hope, so this is a clue that it means ended suddenly. Try your meaning in the sentence: «The rain ended our hopes of a picnic» still makes sense, so you have found it.
explain: Snuff is also a powder made from tobacco, which some people sniff up the nose. It is harmful, so never try it. The phrase «up to snuff» is informal and means good enough, so «Her spelling is up to snuff» means her spelling is good enough.
fact: Snuff can be a verb or a noun.
fact: To snuff out a candle means to put out its flame.
fact: To snuff out something means to stop or end it suddenly, as in «the rain snuffed out our hopes».
fact: Snuff, the powder, is made from tobacco and is harmful to health.
fact: «Up to snuff» is informal and means good enough.
exercise: «She snuffed out the candle before bed.» What does snuffed out mean here? | Carried to the table | *Put out the flame | Wrapped in paper | Lit up brightly
exercise: «The rain snuffed out our hopes of a picnic.» What does snuffed out mean here? | Made the picnic bigger | Made our hopes shine | Sang a song about the picnic | *Ended our hopes suddenly
exercise: Mum says, «The cake is up to snuff.» What does up to snuff mean? | Burnt on the top | *Good enough | Made of tobacco | Too big for the plate
test: Which is the best meaning of snuff in «to snuff a candle»? | To light its flame | To paint it | *To put out its flame | To cut it into pieces
test: Snuff, the powder made from tobacco, is | A kind of cloth | *Harmful to your health | Good for your teeth | A sweet to eat
exam: «The fire was snuffed out by the heavy rain.» Which word means the same as snuffed out? | *Stopped | Lit | Painted | Warmed
